# Docs follow behavior

Update the documentation that owns a change in the same turn — never wait to
be asked. Skip only a typo, a comment, or a formatting change with no
user-visible effect.

- Repository Markdown is English; chat with the user may be Polish
  (`english-docs`).
- Where a draft index exists, `drafts/99.NEEDS-ATTENTION.md` is the canonical
  status index: mark resolved items `[x]` (with a commit SHA when code lands)
  and keep `Decide first` agreeing with the numbered sections.
- Drafts are local reasoning, not shipped specifications. Do not move one
  into a product, ops, or infra repository.
- Do not bump remotes, commit, push, or deploy unless the user explicitly
  asks.

| The change | Update |
| --- | --- |
| Repository layout, or a new checkout | the owning `mani.yaml`, `README.md`, and `AGENTS.md` |
| Product behavior or a public API | that product's `README.md` (and `CHANGELOG.md` where a hook owns it) |
| An open decision | the owning draft and the Draft 99 index, in one edit |
| A local port / URL / secret surface | the docs file that maps it, and the config that binds it |

A nested workspace or product may keep its own, narrower `docs-sync` for its
own files; this rule is the floor, not the ceiling.
